ags` if the\n264 |     estimator is a regressor, otherwise it will be set to ``None``.\n265 | \n266 |     Parameters\n267 |     ----------\n268 |     estimator : estimator object\n269 |         The estimator for which to get the default tags.\n270 | \n271 |     Returns\n272 |     -------\n273 |     tags : Tags\n274 |         The default tags for the estimator.\n275 |     \"\"\"\n276 |     est_is_classifier = getattr(estimator, \"_estimator_type\", None) == \"classifier\"\n277 |     est_is_regressor = getattr(estimator, \"_estimator_type\", None) == \"regressor\"\n278 |     target_required = est_is_classifier or est_is_regressor\n279 | \n280 |     return Tags(\n281 |         estimator_type=getattr(estimator, \"_estimator_type\", None),\n282 |         target_tags=TargetTags(required=target_required),\n283 |         transformer_tags=(\n284 |             TransformerTags()\n285 |             if hasattr(estimator, \"transform\") or hasattr(estimator, \"fit_transform\")\n286 |             else None\n287 |         ),\n288 |         classifier_tags=ClassifierTags() if est_is_classifier else None,\n289 |         regressor_tags=RegressorTags() if est_is_regressor else None,\n290 |     )\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me analyze the code and prepare the locations that need modification to implement the requested feature.\n\n## Step 2: Let's explore the relevant modules and their relationships.\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['BaseEstimator', '__sklearn_tags__', 'Tags']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for term \"BaseEstimator\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `sklearn/base.py:BaseEstimator`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `BaseEstimator`.\nJust show the structure of this class due to response length limitations:\n```\nclass BaseEstimator(_HTMLDocumentationLinkMixin, _MetadataRequeste