          many repeated values.\n3580 |         DataFrame.info : Concise summary of a DataFrame.\n3581 | \n3582 |         Notes\n3583 |         -----\n3584 |         See the :ref:`Frequently Asked Questions <df-memory-usage>` for more\n3585 |         details.\n3586 | \n3587 |         Examples\n3588 |         --------\n3589 |         >>> dtypes = [\"int64\", \"float64\", \"complex128\", \"object\", \"bool\"]\n3590 |         >>> data = dict([(t, np.ones(shape=5000, dtype=int).astype(t)) for t in dtypes])\n3591 |         >>> df = pd.DataFrame(data)\n3592 |         >>> df.head()\n3593 |            int64  float64            complex128  object  bool\n3594 |         0      1      1.0              1.0+0.0j       1  True\n3595 |         1      1      1.0              1.0+0.0j       1  True\n3596 |         2      1      1.0              1.0+0.0j       1  True\n3597 |         3      1      1.0              1.0+0.0j       1  True\n3598 |         4      1      1.0              1.0+0.0j       1  True\n3599 | \n3600 |         >>> df.memory_usage()\n3601 |         Index           128\n3602 |         int64         40000\n3603 |         float64       40000\n3604 |         complex128    80000\n3605 |         object        40000\n3606 |         bool           5000\n3607 |         dtype: int64\n3608 | \n3609 |         >>> df.memory_usage(index=False)\n3610 |         int64         40000\n3611 |         float64       40000\n3612 |         complex128    80000\n3613 |         object        40000\n3614 |         bool           5000\n3615 |         dtype: int64\n3616 | \n3617 |         The memory footprint of `object` dtype columns is ignored by default:\n3618 | \n3619 |         >>> df.memory_usage(deep=True)\n3620 |         Index            128\n3621 |         int64          40000\n3622 |         float64        40000\n3623 |         complex128     80000\n3624 |         object        180000\n3625 |         bool            5000\n3626 |         dtype: int64\n3627 | \n3628 |         Use a Categorical for efficient storage of an object-dtype column with\n3629 |         many repeated values.\n3630 | \n3631 |         >>> df[\"object\"].astype(\"category\").memory_usage(deep=True)\n3632 |         5136\n3633 |         \"\"\"\n3634 |         result = self._constructor_sliced(\n3635 |             [c.memory_usage(index=False, deep=deep) for col, c in self.items()],\n3636 |             index=self.columns,\n3637 |             dtype=np.intp,\n3638 |         )\n3639 |         if index:\n3640 |             index_memory_usage = self._constructor_sliced(\n3641 |                 self.index.memory_usage(deep=deep), index=[\"Index\"]\n3642 |             )\n3643 |             result = index_memory_usage._append(result)\n3644 |         return result\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"PandasDEVELOPER CONTRIBUTING\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound code snippet in file `doc/sphinxext/announce.py`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n  1 | #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  2 | \"\"\"\n  3 | Script to generate contributor and pull request lists\n  4 | \n  5 | This script generates contributor and pull request lists for release\n  6 | announcements using GitHub v3 protocol. Use requires an authentication token in\n  7 | order to have sufficient bandwidth, you can get one following the directions at\n  8 | `<https://help.github.com/articles/creating-an-access-token-for-command-line-use/>_\n  9 | Don't add any scope, as the default is read access to public information. The\n 10 | token may be stored in an environment variable as you only get one chance to\n 11 | see it.\n 12 | \n 13 | Usage::\n 14 | \n 15 |     $ ./scripts/announce.py <token> <revision range>\n 16 | \n 17 | The output is utf8 rst.\n 18 | \n 19 | Dependencies\n 20 | ------------\n 21 | \n 22 | - gitpython\n 23 | - pygithub\n 24 | \n 25 | Some code was copied from scipy `tools/gh_lists.py` and `tools/authors.py`.\n 26 | \n 27 | Examples\n 28 | --------\n 29 | \n 30 | From the bash command line with $GITHUB token.\n 31 | \n 32 |     $ ./scripts/announce.py $GITHUB v1.11.0..v1.11.1 > announce.rst\n 33 | \n 34 | \"\"\"\n 35 | \n 36 | import codecs\n 37 | import os\n 38 | import re\n 39 | import textwrap\n 40 | \n 41 | from git import Repo\n 42 | \n 43 | # Contributors to be renamed.\n 44 | CONTRIBUTOR_MAPPING = {\"znkjnffrezna\": \"znetbgcubravk\"}\n 45 | \n 46 | UTF8Writer = codecs.getwriter(\"utf8\")\n 47 | this_repo = Repo(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\"))\n 48 | \n 49 | author_msg = \"\"\"\\\n 50 | A total of %d people contributed patches to this release.  People with a\n 51 | \"+\" by their names contributed a patch for the first time.\n 52 | \"\"\"\n 53 | \n 54 | pull_request_msg = \"\"\"\\\n 55 | A total of %d pull requests were merged for this release.\n 56 | \"\"\"\n```\n\nFound class `pandas/_typing.py:ReadBuffer`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n290 | class ReadBuffer(BaseBuffer, Protocol[AnyStr_co]):\n291 |     def read(self, __n: int = ...) -> AnyStr_co:\n292 |         # for BytesIOWrapper, gzip.GzipFile, bz2.BZ2File\n293 |         ...\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me analyze the code and locate the specific areas that need modification.\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['Can only use .str accessor with string values!', 'inferred_dtype']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\npandas/core/strings/accessor.py:StringMethods._validate\npandas/core/arrays/arrow/accessors.py:StructAccessor._is_valid_pyarrow_dtype\npandas/core/arrays/arrow/accessors.py:StructAccessor\npandas/core/arrays/arrow/accessors.py:StructAccessor.__init__\npandas/core/arrays/arrow/accessors.py:ListAccessor.__init__\npandas/core/arrays/arrow/accessors.py:ListAccessor\npandas/core/arrays/arrow/accessors.py:ListAccessor._is_valid_pyarrow_dtype\npandas/core/algorithms.p