n1892 | \n1893 |     Returns\n1894 |     -------\n1895 |     inferred_dtype : str\n1896 |         The string for the inferred dtype from _libs.lib.infer_dtype\n1897 |     values : np.ndarray\n1898 |         An array of object dtype that will be inferred to have\n1899 |         `inferred_dtype`\n1900 | \n1901 |     Examples\n1902 |     --------\n1903 |     >>> from pandas._libs import lib\n1904 |     >>>\n1905 |     >>> def test_something(any_skipna_inferred_dtype):\n1906 |     ...     inferred_dtype, values = any_skipna_inferred_dtype\n1907 |     ...     # will pass\n1908 |     ...     assert lib.infer_dtype(values, skipna=True) == inferred_dtype\n1909 |     \"\"\"\n1910 |     inferred_dtype, values = request.param\n1911 |     values = np.array(values, dtype=object)  # object dtype to avoid casting\n1912 | \n1913 |     # correctness of inference tested in tests/dtypes/test_inference.py\n1914 |     return inferred_dtype, values\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"inferred_dtype\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `asv_bench/benchmarks/index_cached_properties.py:IndexCache.time_inferred_type`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n71 | def time_inferred_type(self, index_type):\n72 |         self.idx.inferred_type\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/dtypes/missing.py:construct_1d_array_from_inferred_fill_value`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n577 | def construct_1d_array_from_inferred_fill_value(\n578 |     value: object, length: int\n579 | ) -> ArrayLike:\n580 |     # Find our empty_value dtype by constructing an array\n581 |     #  from our value and doing a .take on it\n582 |     from pandas.core.algorithms import take_nd\n583 |     from pandas.core.construction import sanitize_array\n584 |     from pandas.core.indexes.base import Index\n585 | \n586 |     arr = sanitize_array(value, Index(range(1)), copy=False)\n587 |     taker = -1 * np.ones(length, dtype=np.intp)\n588 |     return take_nd(arr, taker)\n```\n\