single value to place all points in the same plane.\n2919 |         zdir : {'x', 'y', 'z', '-x', '-y', '-z'}, default: 'z'\n2920 |             The axis direction for the *zs*. This is useful when plotting 2D\n2921 |             data on a 3D Axes. The data must be passed as *xs*, *ys*. Setting\n2922 |             *zdir* to 'y' then plots the data to the x-z-plane.\n2923 | \n2924 |             See also :doc:`/gallery/mplot3d/2dcollections3d`.\n2925 | \n2926 |         s : float or array-like, default: 20\n2927 |             The marker size in points**2. Either an array of the same length\n2928 |             as *xs* and *ys* or a single value to make all markers the same\n2929 |             size.\n2930 |         c : :mpltype:`color`, sequence, or sequence of colors, optional\n2931 |             The marker color. Possible values:\n2932 | \n2933 |             - A single color format string.\n2934 |             - A sequence of colors of length n.\n2935 |             - A sequence of n numbers to be mapped to colors using *cmap* and\n2936 |               *norm*.\n2937 |             - A 2D array in which the rows are RGB or RGBA.\n2938 | \n2939 |             For more details see the *c* argument of `~.axes.Axes.scatter`.\n2940 |         depthshade : bool, default: True\n2941 |             Whether to shade the scatter markers to give the appearance of\n2942 |             depth. Each call to ``scatter()`` will perform its depthshading\n2943 |             independently.\n2944 |         axlim_clip : bool, default: False\n2945 |             Whether to hide the scatter points outside the axes view limits.\n2946 | \n2947 |             .. versionadded:: 3.10\n2948 |         data : indexable object, optional\n2949 |             DATA_PARAMETER_PLACEHOLDER\n2950 |         **kwargs\n2951 |             All other keyword arguments are passed on to `~.axes.Axes.scatter`.\n2952 | \n2953 |         Returns\n2954 |         -------\n2955 |         paths : `~matplotlib.collections.PathCollection`