"function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for term \"pandas/core/internals/blocks.py:Block.interpolate\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/internals/blocks.py:Block.interpolate`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `pandas/core/internals/blocks.py:Block.interpolate`.\n```\n1362 | def interpolate(\n1363 |         self,\n1364 |         *,\n1365 |         method: InterpolateOptions,\n1366 |         index: Index,\n1367 |         inplace: bool = False,\n1368 |         limit: int | None = None,\n1369 |         limit_direction: Literal[\"forward\", \"backward\", \"both\"] = \"forward\",\n1370 |         limit_area: Literal[\"inside\", \"outside\"] | None = None,\n1371 |         **kwargs,\n1372 |     ) -> list[Block]:\n1373 |         inplace = validate_bool_kwarg(inplace, \"inplace\")\n1374 |         # error: Non-overlapping equality check [...]\n1375 |         if method == \"asfreq\":  # type: ignore[comparison-overlap]\n1376 |             # clean_fill_method used to allow this\n1377 |             missing.clean_fill_method(method)\n1378 | \n1379 |         if not self._can_hold_na:\n1380 |             # If there are no NAs, then interpolate is a no-op\n1381 |             return [self.copy(deep=False)]\n1382 | \n1383 |         if self.dtype == _dtype_obj:\n1384 |             # GH#53631\n1385 |             name = {1: \"Series\", 2: \"DataFrame\"}[self.ndim]\n1386 |             raise TypeError(f\"{name} cannot interpolate with object dtype.\")\n1387 | \n1388 |         copy, refs = self._get_refs_and_copy(inplace)\n1389 | \n1390 |         # Dispatch to the EA method.\n1391 |         new_values = self.array_values.interpolate(\n1392 |             method=method,\n1393 |             axis=self.ndim - 1,\n1394 |             index=index,\n1395 |             limit=limit,\n1396 |             limit_direction=limit_direction,\n1397 |             limit_area=limit_area,\