"\n1150 |         Convert times to midnight.\n1151 | \n1152 |         The time component of the date-time is converted to midnight i.e.\n1153 |         00:00:00. This is useful in cases, when the time does not matter.\n1154 |         Length is unaltered. The timezones are unaffected.\n1155 | \n1156 |         This method is available on Series with datetime values under\n1157 |         the ``.dt`` accessor, and directly on Datetime Array/Index.\n1158 | \n1159 |         Returns\n1160 |         -------\n1161 |         DatetimeArray, DatetimeIndex or Series\n1162 |             The same type as the original data. Series will have the same\n1163 |             name and index. DatetimeIndex will have the same name.\n1164 | \n1165 |         See Also\n1166 |         --------\n1167 |         floor : Floor the datetimes to the specified freq.\n1168 |         ceil : Ceil the datetimes to the specified freq.\n1169 |         round : Round the datetimes to the specified freq.\n1170 | \n1171 |         Examples\n1172 |         --------\n1173 |         >>> idx = pd.date_range(\n1174 |         ...     start=\"2014-08-01 10:00\", freq=\"h\", periods=3, tz=\"Asia/Calcutta\"\n1175 |         ... )\n1176 |         >>> idx\n1177 |         DatetimeIndex(['2014-08-01 10:00:00+05:30',\n1178 |                        '2014-08-01 11:00:00+05:30',\n1179 |                        '2014-08-01 12:00:00+05:30'],\n1180 |                         dtype='datetime64[ns, Asia/Calcutta]', freq='h')\n1181 |         >>> idx.normalize()\n1182 |         DatetimeIndex(['2014-08-01 00:00:00+05:30',\n1183 |                        '2014-08-01 00:00:00+05:30',\n1184 |                        '2014-08-01 00:00:00+05:30'],\n1185 |                        dtype='datetime64[ns, Asia/Calcutta]', freq=None)\n1186 |         \"\"\"\n1187 |         new_values = normalize_i8_timestamps(self.asi8, self.tz, reso=self._creso)\n1188 |         dt64_values = new_values.view(self._ndarray.dtype)\n1189 | \n1190 |         dta = type(self).