w from a single column will produce a single\n926 |         scalar DataFrame:\n927 | \n928 |         >>> df_0a = df.loc[df.index < 1, [\"a\"]]\n929 |         >>> df_0a\n930 |            a\n931 |         0  1\n932 | \n933 |         Squeezing the rows produces a single scalar Series:\n934 | \n935 |         >>> df_0a.squeeze(\"rows\")\n936 |         a    1\n937 |         Name: 0, dtype: int64\n938 | \n939 |         Squeezing all axes will project directly into a scalar:\n940 | \n941 |         >>> df_0a.squeeze()\n942 |         1\n943 |         \"\"\"\n944 |         axes = range(self._AXIS_LEN) if axis is None else (self._get_axis_number(axis),)\n945 |         result = self.iloc[\n946 |             tuple(\n947 |                 0 if i in axes and len(a) == 1 else slice(None)\n948 |                 for i, a in enumerate(self.axes)\n949 |             )\n950 |         ]\n951 |         if isinstance(result, NDFrame):\n952 |             result = result.__finalize__(self, method=\"squeeze\")\n953 |         return result\n```\n\nFound class `pandas/core/frame.py:DataFrame`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nJust show the structure of this class due to response length limitations:\n```\nclass DataFrame(NDFrame, OpsMixin):\n\n    _internal_names_set = {\"columns\", \"index\"} | NDFrame._internal_names_set\n    _typ = \"dataframe\"\n    _HANDLED_TYPES = (Series, Index, ExtensionArray, np.ndarray)\n    _accessors: set[str] = {\"sparse\"}\n    _hidden_attrs: frozenset[str] = NDFrame._hidden_attrs | frozenset([])\n    _mgr: BlockManager\n\n    # similar to __array_priority__, positions DataFrame before Series, Index,\n    #  and ExtensionArray.  Should NOT be overridden by subclasses.\n    __pandas_priority__ = 4000\n\n    @property\n    def _constructor(self) -> type[DataFrame]:\n...\n    def _constructor_from_mgr(self, mgr, axes) -> DataFrame:\n...\n    _constructor_sliced: Callable[..., Series] = Series\n\n    def _constructor_sliced_from_mgr(self, mgr, axes